note Translated from go src/encoding/csv/reader.go, nextRune (lines 292 to 295).

note GAP: a Unicode code point type - Go's rune; the doc has Text and Bytes but no character or code point type, so Rune is assumed to exist
note GAP: utf8.DecodeRune returns two values (the rune and its byte width) and never fails: empty or invalid input gives U+FFFD with width 0 or 1; the record below stands in for the pair
type Decoded_rune
    field rune as a Rune
    field size as a Nat

to decode_rune b
    given b is Bytes
    produces a Decoded_rune

to next_rune b
    given b is Bytes
    produces a Rune

    note WORKAROUND: Go discards the second result with `_`; Scribe has no discard or destructuring, so the whole record is bound and one field read
    let decoded be decode_rune b
    give back rune of decoded
